## High-Yield Process and Map Examples (7 rows)

These are the kinds of process and map examples IELTS Writing Task 1
uses most often.

1. **Desalination process** — multi-stage flash distillation or reverse
   osmosis used in Qatar.
2. **LNG production** — liquefied natural gas from the North Field.
3. **Solar panel manufacturing** — from silicon wafer to finished
   panel.
4. **Water recycling** — used water to drinking water.
5. **Lusail City development** — from 2010 (undeveloped) to 2025
   (urban centre).
6. **Education City development** — from 2000 (few buildings) to 2024
   (international universities).
7. **Hamad International Airport development** — from 2010
   (under construction) to 2025 (major hub).

## Previous Year Patterns (IELTS 2018–2025)

IELTS Writing Task 1 process and map questions have been used since
2018. Over 2018–2025:

- 2018–2020: Process diagrams were more common (12-15% of tests); maps
  were rare (3-5% of tests).
- 2021–2023: Process diagrams stabilized at 10-12% of tests; maps
  increased to 5-8% of tests.
- 2024–2025: Process diagrams at 10-12% of tests; maps at 5-8% of tests.

The pattern: IELTS Writing Task 1 process and map questions have
stabilized at 15-20% of all Task 1 questions since 2021. Candidates
who practice both process and map outperform those who focus only on
data-comparison.

## Pro Tips (10 enumeration)

1. **Identify the visual type first.** Process or map.
2. **Use present simple passive for process diagrams.** *"The metal is
   heated"* (NOT *"They heat the metal"*).
3. **Use past tense for maps.** *"A hospital was built"* (NOT *"A
   hospital is built"*).
4. **Use sequenced language.** First, then, subsequently, finally.
5. **Use directional vocabulary for maps.** North, south, east, west;
   on the left, on the right.
6. **Write an overview (1-2 sentences).** Identify the key feature.
7. **Write 2-3 body paragraphs.** One paragraph per stage-group.
8. **Use varied vocabulary.** Do not repeat the same verbs.
9. **Aim for 170-200 words.** Not less than 150 words.
10. **Reserve 5 minutes for review.** Do not submit without review.

